SHAIK RESHMA - Jul 2, 2026

File Name: cms_service.dart

1. Modification Done:

   * Created a `CommunityStats` data model for homepage numbers (alumni, batches, events, members).
   * Added `fetchStats()` to request stats from `GET /api/v1/cms/stats` when available.
   * Added fallback default values (15,000+ alumni, 60+ batches, etc.) when the API is not ready or fails.
   * Marks whether stats came from the API or from local defaults.

2. Purpose of This Modification:

   * Phase 1 handbook expects homepage stats to load from the API when possible.
   * The backend CMS stats endpoint is not built yet, so fallback values keep the page working during development.

3. How This Modification Is Involved in the Flow:

   * Called from `home_screen.dart` on page load alongside the health check.
   * Results are passed to `stats_section.dart` to display community numbers.
   * When the backend adds `/cms/stats`, the same code will automatically show live data without changing the Home screen.
